      "aliases": [
        "LSR"
      ],
      "description": "Line status register: the transmitter and receiver state and the receive errors.",
      "behaviour": "Bit 0 data ready, 1 overrun, 2 parity error, 3 framing error, 4 break, 5 transmit holding register empty, 6 transmitter empty. A read clears bits 1 to 4 and the line status interrupt.",
      "differs": "MAME lets a write set the status bits and raise their interrupts; DOSBox-X treats a write as a reserved register.",
