      "key": "0x06",
      "name": "modem status",
      "aliases": [
        "MSR"
      ],
      "description": "Modem status register: the modem input lines and their changes.",
      "behaviour": "Bits 7 to 4 are DCD, RI, DSR and CTS. Bits 3, 1 and 0 flag a change of DCD, DSR and CTS, and bit 2 flags the trailing edge of RI. A read clears the change bits and the modem status interrupt; in loopback the bits follow the modem control outputs.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "role": "documentation",
          "ref": "rbil61:PORTS.B 03FE modem status",
          "cites": "03FE  R-  modem status register (MSR) (see #P0883)"
